## TEST 3 — Stop Backend A

| Field | Value |
|-------|-------|
| **Fault type** | Backend failure |
| **Layer** | Application (nginx upstream) |
| **Who acts** | Mac 3 — Krishiv stops Backend A |
| **Fault** | Backend A process stopped on 10.7.10.0:3001 |
| **Reversible** | Yes — Krishiv restarts the process |

### Initial State
- Backend A: HTTP 200, X-Backend: A ✅
- Backend B: HTTP 200, X-Backend: B ✅
- Round-robin: A, B, A, B

### Fault Injection
Mac 3 (Krishiv) stops Backend A server process.

### Test Command (Mac 2)
```zsh
for i in {1..4}; do
  curl -s --max-time 5 --cacert configs/tls/team1.test.crt \
    --resolve app.team1.test:8443:10.7.17.151 \
    https://app.team1.test:8443/api/status
  echo ""
done
```

### Observed Output
```
[FILL from evidence/script8/test3_stop_backend_a/test3_*.txt]
```

### Expected Output
```
{"backend": "B", "status": "ok"}
{"backend": "B", "status": "ok"}
{"backend": "B", "status": "ok"}
{"backend": "B", "status": "ok"}
```
All requests go to B only. nginx detects A is unreachable and stops sending to it.

### Layer Analysis
| Layer | Status | Observation |
|-------|--------|-------------|
| DNS | ✅ OK | Resolves correctly |
| TCP (client→nginx) | ✅ OK | nginx accepts connection |
| TLS | ✅ OK | Handshake completes |
| Application (nginx→A) | ❌ FAILED | Connection refused on 10.7.10.0:3001 |
| Application (nginx→B) | ✅ OK | nginx fails over to B |

### Cause
nginx uses round-robin with passive health checking. When Backend A refuses connections, nginx marks it as failed and routes all traffic to Backend B. The client sees no error — the failover is transparent.

### Restore
Krishiv restarts Backend A. nginx automatically re-adds it to rotation.

**Restored:** [ ] Confirmed — round-robin A/B resumes

**Evidence file:** `evidence/script8/test3_stop_backend_a/test3_*.txt`

